{"episode_id": "51e72480df3e", "role": "orchestrator", "agent_id": "orchestrator", "dispatch_id": null, "group_id": null, "arbitration_id": null, "step": 35, "call_id": "call-35", "name": "reply", "t_start": 1792140453.3964338, "t_end": 1792140453.396617, "exit_code": null, "timed_out": false, "is_error": false, "output_chars": 25, "tool_call_id": "call_resp_01a143e4-f603-738a-b3d3-7f34dbd2e54d_0", "arguments": {"done": true, "text": "All three fixed:\n1. A required flag no longer gets an implicit `False` default, so `--on/--off` with `required=True` now errors with \"Missing option '--on'\" when not given (`--on`/`--off` still work).\n2. `click.echo` (and `err=True`), the progress bar and the pager now silently drop output when there is no stream (pythonw.exe / no console) instead of raising `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'write'`.\n3. A flag with a `flag_value` and an `envvar` now uses the configured `flag_value` when the variable is set: `UPPER=whatever cmd` prints `upper`.\nFull test suite: 488 passed, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed (unchanged from baseline).", "to": 1}}
{"episode_id": "51e72480df3e", "role": "orchestrator", "agent_id": "orchestrator", "dispatch_id": null, "group_id": null, "arbitration_id": null, "step": 35, "call_id": "call-35", "name": "reply", "t_start": 1792140453.396769, "t_end": 1792140453.396866, "exit_code": null, "timed_out": false, "is_error": false, "output_chars": 25, "tool_call_id": "call_resp_01a143e4-f603-738a-b3d3-7f34dbd2e54d_1", "arguments": {"done": true, "text": "All three fixed:\n1. `click.argument(..., cls=...)` / `click.option(..., cls=...)` no longer consume `cls` from the shared attrs dict, so the same decorator can be applied to several commands and each gets your custom class.\n2. `click.Path(resolve_path=True)` now resolves relative symlink targets against the link's directory (uses `os.path.realpath` alone), so `/tmp/demo/link -> real.txt` yields `/tmp/demo/real.txt` instead of `/real.txt`.\n3. The help text now takes `default_map` into account: with `default_map={\"foo\": {\"name\": True}}`, `foo --help` shows `[default: name]`, matching the value the flag actually takes.\nFull test suite: 488 passed, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed (unchanged from baseline).", "to": 2}}
